WEBVTT

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:17.380
Now that was an awful match!

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.350
The audience is in an uproar!

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:21.430
Angry spectators are now throwing their seat cushions!

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:22.810
Yabuki, you bastard!

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:24.810
Get the hell out, Yabuki Joe!

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:29.320
And the match is over! Yabuki has been defeated!

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:31.150
That's his third straight loss!

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:33.940
A decisive third straight loss!

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:16.820
Well, Nishi, I think I've given up completely.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:21.450
We've done all we could do.

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:29.800
I dreamed of raising Joe to be a world champion.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:32.330
Sure, it was brief,

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:34.460
but at least I got to dream.

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:41.430
Well, Joe's still young, you know!

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:43.680
And there's more to life than boxing.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:56.550
Dear, come and eat your breakfast so we can open the store!

00:03:56.550 --> 00:04:00.470
I know, already! Why do you think I'm brushing my teeth?

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:02.600
Just make it quick!

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:06.300
We can't keep our customers waiting to buy their breakfast side dishes!

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.810
Now how do you like that?

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:11.140
I'm getting ordered around in my own family business!

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:14.320
We're just short on hands, that's all.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:22.870
Even the news is outright depressing!

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:23.400
Dear!

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.660
I know! I'm coming already!

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.160
Seconds!

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:31.540
Here's your tea.

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:34.120
I didn't ask for more tea! I asked for more rice!

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.630
Two bowls is enough. Now, open the store.

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:39.880
Just gimme some rice!

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.670
Noriko! Hey, Noriko!

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:45.760
Come down for breakfast right now! You'll be late for school!

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:47.430
Noriko! Noriko! Noriko!

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.230
Noriko! Noriko! Noriko!

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:50.430
Noriko! Noriko! Noriko!

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.430
Do you want to be late for school, Noriko?

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:54.650
Noriko!

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:56.400
Coming!

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:00.150
I'm going now.

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.570
Noriko, what about breakfast?

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:03.870
It's fine. I've lost my appetite.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:12.000
Poor thing! She can't even eat cause you keep nagging her like that!

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:12.870
What was that?

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:15.710
Oh, just saying you got a lot of class.{need TLC on this, "class" makes no sense here}

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:19.380
Well, excuse me for being "classy"! This is just how I am!

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.960
Now go and open the store already!

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:21.680
Take this!

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:24.970
Now that's funny! Are you picking a fight with me? {No scene change - ninja}

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.470
Damn right I am!

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:27.640
Damn broad!

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.360
Say that again, you little...

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:29.360
<i>Shut up!</i>

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:32.520
I'm in a bad mood today! You're in for it now!

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:34.150
You're dead wrong if you think you can defy me!

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:36.150
Now give up already and go open the store!

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:36.150
<i>Shut up!</i>

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:38.870
How do you expect me to care about the store when Joe's in trouble?

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:38.870
<i>So what?</i>

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:39.890
Joe's done for now!

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.610
Now you've done it, woman!

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:47.990
Yabuki-kun...

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:05.220
Oh, right! Emergency meeting! Emergency meeting!

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:06.260
I've gotta hurry!

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:12.690
Hey! Good morning, guys!

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.530
Sorry for being so late, everyone.

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:24.110
I'm really not what you'd call a morning person, you see...

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:27.160
Do you even realize how important this morning's meeting is?

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:29.280
I repent. Do what you must.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:35.740
That aside, Bro Joe is facing his greatest crisis ever!

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:38.920
And that makes it our crisis!

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:40.590
Exactly!

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:43.280
It's so big a crisis, it's a mega-crisis!

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:48.720
I can't believe my darling Joe could lose three matches by KO in a row...

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:50.970
It's just so drool!

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:52.770
I think you mean "cruel," Sachi...

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:55.310
It's just so drool! Poor man...

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:58.900
I'm sure... I'm sure... he's in a trump...

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:00.400
Y-You mean a slump?

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:01.320
A trump...

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:04.730
Yeah, poor Bro Joe.

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:10.740
Well, for now, we've got to do something for Bro Joe!

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:13.240
I'll do anything for Bro Joe!

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:14.740
I swear it, too!

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:15.750
Me three!

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:16.700
Me four!

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:20.800
Me five...

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:25.590
Hip-hip, hooray!

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:35.470
Welcome, good sir!

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:38.970
Oh, it's just you, Nishi.

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:41.980
Wh-What happened to your face?

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:46.360
Well... I guess you could say this came from some family recreation...

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:51.280
Well, even if I <i>did</i> have to take on my wife's name, I still gotta discipline her! {http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mukoy%C5%8Dshi}

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:53.030
Dear!

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:53.990
Yes?

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:57.100
Help me out! I can't see a thing!

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:58.210
Yes, yes, yes!

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:04.110
Keep your grip on it!

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:06.420
I know, I know!

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:08.550
Oh, Danpei-san's with you, too?

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:09.250
Come on!

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:13.510
I'd like to thank you for everything you've done for Nishi.

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:21.520
Oh, please, Danpei-san! What's this, all of a sudden?

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.770
Well, you see...

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:30.410
What's this? Why are you looking so solemn, Nishi?

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:32.030
What's going on?

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:36.530
Actually, the old man has something to ask you two...

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:41.080
I've got a favor to ask of you.

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:14.440
Me? Retire?{old 'Retire? Me?'}

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:22.830
H-He's laughing!

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:25.040
Bro Joe's laughing to himself!

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:28.050
C-Could he be so sad he's gone crazy?

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:01.190
I saw it, I saw it, I saw it!

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:05.660
Joe's... Bro Joe's training!

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:06.880
Really?

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:10.670
Yeah, really! He's super into it, too!

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:13.670
I-I guess Joe isn't depressed, after all!

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:16.180
All right, let's all go cheer Joe on!

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:19.310
Let's go!

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:23.180
Wait, hold it!

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:27.860
Look, it's the old man and Nishi! Mr. Hayashi is with them too!

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:29.480
So? What's the big deal?

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:33.740
Can't you tell? Just look at them!

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:36.150
Now that you mention it, they're all

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:39.490
looking pretty grim, if you ask me.

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:58.340
Hey! Looks like everyone's here!

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.270
What's with the long faces?

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:07.350
Is something wrong?

00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:09.360
You see, Joe...

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:13.360
I've been talking with Mr. Hayashi here.

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:14.650
Talking?

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:19.200
I've decided to close down Tange Gym as of today.

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:52.100
Close down... Tange Gym?

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:57.280
Which means we'll have to discuss you and Nishi's future.{or "your and Nishi's futures" if separate}

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:01.620
Fortunately, Mr. Hayashi here is going to look after you two.

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:02.700
Look after them?

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:04.610
Oh, not at all! It's the other way around!

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:08.290
You'll be the ones looking after us, Yabuki-kun!

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:12.210
We're so understaffed, the mornings are just hell!

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:19.130
What do you say, Yabuki-kun? Want to turn your part-time job into a full employee position?

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:28.930
What do you say, Joe? Hayashi-san's really concerned about you!

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:32.100
Wanna work at Hayashi-san's with me?

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:34.780
Nishi... Is that what you're gonna do?

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:37.660
You're happy with that?

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:42.460
But Tange Gym's gonna close down, Joe!

00:12:42.460 --> 00:12:44.990
Boxing ain't an option for us anymore.

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:47.490
You're just gonna quit boxing?

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:50.250
Yeah! I quit!

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:52.170
I'm gonna live my life my own way.

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:54.960
Besides, boxing just ain't for me.

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:59.720
I get it. So Nishi's working at Hayashi's, and the old man's closing down the gym.{I see vs. I get it}

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:01.260
I get it.

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:04.970
I get it, but that's not okay with me.

00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:15.010
Joe! What are you gonna do?

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:16.940
I wonder.

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:18.770
I don't even know myself.

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:23.780
All I know is that there's no chance in hell I'm giving up boxing!

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:37.460
I'm going out for a little run.

00:13:47.810 --> 00:13:51.140
Bro Joe! Wait! Bro Joe!

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:04.780
Hey, wait!

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:07.530
Wait up, Bro Joe!

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:09.360
Bro Joe! Wait!

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:32.850
Bro Joe's so mean! He didn't have to run off like that!

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:35.770
What are you talking about, idiot? Bro Joe's running as fast as he can

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:37.680
because he's just that into his training!

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:43.690
But why are they closing down the gym when Bro Joe's so into it?

00:14:43.990 --> 00:14:46.940
That's it! I won't stand for that!

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:48.450
Yeah!

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:49.820
Never!

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:51.570
We won't stand for it!

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:00.290
Tange Gym's closing!

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:01.920
We oppose it!

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:04.250
We oppose Yabuki Joe retiring!

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.970
We oppose Yabuki Joe retiring!

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:09.010
Coach Tange should reflect upon his actions!

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:11.500
Coach Tange should reflect upon his actions!

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:12.930
Hup, two!

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:13.890
Hup, two!

00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:14.850
Retirement!

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:15.510
No way!

00:15:15.510 --> 00:15:16.640
Retirement!

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:17.520
No way!

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:18.310
Closing!

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:19.150
No way!

00:15:19.150 --> 00:15:20.100
Closing!

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:20.770
No way!

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:21.570
Hayashi's!

00:15:21.570 --> 00:15:22.600
No way!

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:23.240
Hayashi's!

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:23.940
No way!

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:24.820
Retirement!

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:25.650
<i>Old man!</i>

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:25.650
No way!

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:26.450
Retirement!

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:27.480
No way!

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:28.160
Mammoth!

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:29.070
No way!

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:29.990
Mammoth!

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:30.950
No way!

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:31.870
<i>Cut it out!</i>

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:31.870
Retirement!

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:32.620
No way!

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:33.490
Retirement!

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:34.330
No way!

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:35.160
Retirement!

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:36.160
No way!

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:36.910
Closing!

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:37.750
No way!

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:38.580
Closing!

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:39.420
No way!

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:40.170
Retirement!

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:41.040
No way!

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:41.670
Retirement!

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:42.710
No way!

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:43.590
Closing!

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:44.840
No way!

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:04.280
I see you're working hard, Yabuki-kun!

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:10.690
Who exactly are you?

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:12.700
Oh, me?

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:15.120
Here's my card.

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:17.740
Local Entertainment of Japan...?{need to decide on a name for this}

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:19.920
Yes. Local Entertainment of Japan.

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:21.750
I'm sure you've heard of us.

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:23.750
Nope, never.

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.130
You haven't, have you?

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:28.760
Well, you <i>had</i> been a professional boxer up until yesterday.

00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:30.260
So no wonder you haven't heard of us.

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:32.460
Wait, "had been"?

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:33.510
Hey!

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:35.720
You're talking as if I've already retired!

00:16:36.350 --> 00:16:39.270
I'm sorry... You mean you haven't retired yet?

00:16:39.270 --> 00:16:41.020
Damn right I haven't, asshole!

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:43.520
Joe's the champion of Namida Bridge!

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:46.020
Joe's the champion of Namida Bridge!

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:48.520
Joe's the hero of Namida Bridge!

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:52.530
Joe's the hero of Namida Bridge!

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:54.950
Namida Bridge?

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:56.530
Namida Bridge, huh?{can use "The Bridge of Tears" here to clarify the reference}

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.630
"Let's cross the Bridge of Tears in the opposite direction."

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:10.970
That's what I said to drag Joe and Nishi into boxing...

00:17:10.970 --> 00:17:13.640
And now I'm the one taking boxing away from them!

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:16.810
What kind of a man am I?

00:17:18.060 --> 00:17:20.560
I'm sorry, Nishi! Joe!

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:23.520
What are you talking about, old man?

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:26.020
There's nothing to apologize for.

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:27.980
Take a look at my face.

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:32.030
I'm happy to go to Hayashi-san's!

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:35.700
I wouldn't have that option if it weren't for you.

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:37.530
I'm really grateful to you!

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:40.530
Yeah, I know that this is all really hard on Joe right now.

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:41.540
But you know what, old man?

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:43.870
I'm sure Joe will understand someday!

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:48.510
You're closing the gym to save Joe from this hell, aren't you?

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:52.830
Do you think Yabuki-kun will really understand?

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:55.510
Noriko-han?

00:17:56.160 --> 00:17:59.510
No... He has to understand.

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:15.490
<i>You see, Local Entertainment of Japan is a touring grass-lot boxing league.{sideshow boxing?}{}{}{}{}{}{}{}</i>

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:16.740
<i>Grass-lot boxing?</i>

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:21.580
<i>Yeah. We set up rings and do fights at shrines out in the boonies.</i>

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:25.920
<i>If you're interested, come to the address written on that card.</i>

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:27.290
<i>Sorry for the interruption!</i>

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:00.950
You want something?

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:06.040
You seem to be enjoying yourself, Yabuki-kun.

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:08.250
I'm trying hard to enjoy myself.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:12.040
People keep showing up worrying about what I'll do with my life.

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:15.040
Shouldn't a man be more determined than that?

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:22.010
I just saw the kids shouting in front of the gym.

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:23.600
The kids?

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:29.520
They don't want to see you quit. You're their dream! Their treasure!

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:34.110
I understand how they feel so well it hurts.

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:36.240
But dreams are just dreams.

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:38.360
This is reality, Yabuki-kun!

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:40.700
You need to step back and see the big picture!

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:45.030
I think I've always been seeing the big picture.

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:47.250
No! You're lying!

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:50.540
Have you ever thought of anything besides boxing?

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:04.100
I see. Now that you put it that way, you're right.

00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:07.510
That's been especially true since Rikiishi died.

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:11.020
I'm sorry for raising my voice.

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:18.020
L-Listen, I just think there's more to life than boxing.

00:20:18.740 --> 00:20:21.030
There's far more to life than that!

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:25.500
Our store may be small, but you can live working modestly and steadily...

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:29.790
Yeah. That's one way to live my life...

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:32.040
A laid-back and happy life.

00:20:34.590 --> 00:20:39.090
But you know, Nori-chan, Yabuki Joe has never lived like that.

00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:47.390
What you just said made it all clear to me.

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:50.520
If you take boxing away from me, I'll have nothing left.

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:55.940
I'm sure about it now. I can't run away from boxing!

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:09.620
Yabuki-kun!

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:11.960
Yabuki-kun!

00:21:11.960 --> 00:21:13.580
There's someone who wants to talk to me.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:15.090
I'm gonna go see him.

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:45.650
Don't do this, Joe! P-Please, don't do this!

00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:48.040
Too late, old man.

00:21:48.040 --> 00:21:51.160
I've already signed the contract.

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:55.660
Do you have any idea what touring grass-lot boxing is like?

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:58.920
Yeah, I've got the gist of it.

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:04.640
You idiot! Touring's for down-on-their-luck boxers and no-name rookies...

00:22:04.640 --> 00:22:08.140
Yeah, I know. They're just shows put on for local audiences.

00:22:08.890 --> 00:22:11.270
You know all that...

00:22:11.270 --> 00:22:13.430
And you're still going to do it!?

00:22:14.230 --> 00:22:16.390
Yeah, Joe! You don't have to go that far!

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:18.770
Cut it out, you two.

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:20.110
I'm serious about this!

00:22:20.820 --> 00:22:23.780
Listen! I don't care that it's a wandering side show

00:22:23.780 --> 00:22:25.070
or if it's on some grass lot,

00:22:25.070 --> 00:22:26.700
I just want to go where there's a ring!

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:28.910
I want to box in the ring!

00:22:52.600 --> 00:22:54.310
What's with that look, guys?

00:22:54.310 --> 00:22:55.600
Smile for me!

00:22:55.600 --> 00:22:57.150
Be happy for me!

00:22:57.150 --> 00:22:59.900
I'm gonna start over from square one!

00:22:59.900 --> 00:23:01.990
I'm getting a fresh start!

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:17.500
Hey, Joe, where are you going?

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:18.880
Lots of different places.

00:23:18.880 --> 00:23:21.500
I'm gonna go all over Japan.

00:23:22.380 --> 00:23:25.050
So when will you be back?

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:26.720
I don't know.

00:23:26.720 --> 00:23:29.050
That's not fair!

00:23:29.050 --> 00:23:31.640
But by the time I'm back...

00:23:31.640 --> 00:23:33.430
I'll be strong for real.

00:23:35.100 --> 00:23:36.810
Truly strong.

00:24:02.960 --> 00:24:06.040
Yuke kouya wo

00:24:02.960 --> 00:24:06.040
Go to the wilderness!

00:24:07.090 --> 00:24:09.840
Oira boxer

00:24:07.090 --> 00:24:09.840
I am a boxer.

00:24:10.630 --> 00:24:17.600
Yuuhi ga giragira otoko no yume wa

00:24:10.630 --> 00:24:17.600
The evening sun glitters upon the dreams of men!

00:24:19.310 --> 00:24:23.270
Minna wa kono ore wo nasakemuyo to iu

00:24:19.310 --> 00:24:23.270
Everyone says that I am merciless.

00:24:23.270 --> 00:24:25.310
Tsuki ni hoete hitori

00:24:23.270 --> 00:24:25.310
Howling at the moon alone.

00:24:27.400 --> 00:24:31.530
Oyanashi yadonashi no na mo nai boxer wa

00:24:27.400 --> 00:24:31.530
A parentless, homeless, nameless boxer

00:24:31.530 --> 00:24:34.530
Kusari wo kamikitta Yeah Yeah!

00:24:31.530 --> 00:24:34.530
has bitten off his chains! Yeah, yeah!

00:24:36.240 --> 00:24:39.160
Yuke kouya wo

00:24:36.240 --> 00:24:39.160
Go to the wilderness!

00:24:40.370 --> 00:24:42.910
Oira boxer

00:24:40.370 --> 00:24:42.910
I am a boxer.

00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:51.130
Asahi ga noboru yo otoko no mune ni {removed the Woo, but otherwise japanese is unchanged - Reed}

00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:51.130
The morning sun rises upon the hearts of men!

00:24:54.600 --> 00:24:57.180
Joe has vanished from the slums.

00:24:57.180 --> 00:25:00.940
Noriko, Nishi, and the kids run to Ueno Station in panic.

00:25:01.900 --> 00:25:07.190
Now, as Joe sets out for unfamiliar towns on his way to becoming a touring boxer,

00:25:07.190 --> 00:25:08.150
which way is tomorrow!?
